```java
public boolean nameMatches(String firstName, String lastName) {
    List<String> terms = terms(); // normalized query terms
    if (terms.isEmpty()) return true;
    String first = fold(firstName), last = fold(lastName);
    return terms.stream().allMatch(t -> first.contains(t) || last.contains(t));
}
```

Terms: `name.trim().split("\\s+")` then filter empties, fold each term. Note: "leading, trailing, and repeated whitespace are not significant" — trim + split("\\s+") + drop empties handles this. Empty/blank name → no terms → matches everything.

